>
>after a certain amount of time it just sits there and only allows for a
>^C interupt for quitting, otherwise ignores everything else!

This is a problem with some string constants being too short.  I
posted some trivial patches here a long time ago and have since
deleted the source, so I cannot tell you what they were.  Basically in
one of the header files there are some string constants with lengths
like 9 and 20 and 32 and stuff.  Just increase all of these by say 64
and you will definitely cure the bug.  Only two really need to be
modified, but I can't remember which two.  What's a couple hundred
bytes anyway?

